      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Sheru lived deep in the jungle, where he spent his days hunting and napping under banyan trees. One evening, the wind carried the scent of biryani from a nearby village, and Sheru's mouth watered. He had never tasted anything like it, and he decided he must learn to make it himself.\n\nHe crept to the edge of the village and watched an old cook through a window, noting every step: the soaking of rice, the layering of spices, the slow dum on a clay pot. Night after night, Sheru practised in a clearing, using wild herbs and whatever he could gather. His first attempts were disasters—burnt rice, too much chilli, once he added mud by mistake—but he kept trying.\n\nFinally, one monsoon evening, Sheru's biryani turned out perfect: fragrant, golden, with just the right kick. He invited the jungle animals to taste it, and even the sceptical monkeys came back for seconds. From that day on, Sheru was known not as the fiercest hunter, but as the best biryani chef in the forest.\n\n7:25 AM",
